---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Declaration of Trust — Free Online Generator" description="Create a Declaration of Trust / Private Contract Trust online for free. Business trust structure. Answer a few questions, get a completed PDF. No signup.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> <span>›</span> Declaration of Trust</div>
      <h1>Declaration of Trust</h1>
      <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        Create a Private Contract Trust — a business trust agreement where a trustee holds legal title
        to assets for beneficiaries. Massachusetts Trust heritage.
      </p>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
        <a href="/create/declaration-of-trust/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Create Declaration of Trust →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="upl-notice">
        <strong>How it works:</strong> Answer a few questions about your trust — name, settlor, trustee,
        beneficiaries, governing state — and the tool assembles a complete Declaration of Trust from your
        inputs. The PDF is generated entirely in your browser. No data is sent to any server.
      </div>

      <div style="margin-top: 2rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)); gap: 2rem;">
        <div>
          <h3>What it is</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem;">
            A Declaration of Trust (also called a Trust Agreement) creates a trust and states its terms —
            the trust name, the settlor who creates it, the trustee who administers it, the beneficiaries,
            and the property that makes up the trust.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Business trust structure</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem;">
            In a business or Private Contract Trust, a trustee holds legal title to business assets for the
            benefit of beneficiaries. Different states treat these structures differently — consult an
            attorney about the rules that apply to your situation.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Your browser, your data</h3>
          <p style="color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: 0.95rem;">
            Your answers never leave your device. The PDF is generated client-side, so nothing is stored
            on any server.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="upl-notice" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <strong>Not a law firm.</strong> FreeTrustDocs.com is not a law firm and does not provide legal advice.
        This document is a template assembled from information you provide. You should consult a licensed
        attorney in your jurisdiction before signing or filing any legal document. Use of this tool does not
        create an attorney-client relationship.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
